 </details>
 
 **Runtime invariant:** No companion is published. Conversation and Slot registration enforce Chat target consistency.
+
+Client plugins call ctx.chatPresentation.preserveReplies(preset) to keep every reply-bearing Assistant step visible when completed turns fold for that preset. Reasoning within those steps and separate Tool rows still fold. Registrations are effects; disposal restores ordinary behavior. The policy applies equally to live and restored history without changing model requests or the saved work-details preference.
+
+The conversation.chat.turn-actions chain can replace the default fork controls for a complete turn, including one without closing text. It receives the bound sessionId and agentPreset, the turn and its raw closing coordinate. Selectors remain pure functions of their owner props.
+
+The conversation.chat.user-actions list adds actions beside a user bubble and supplies its raw message sequence. Persisted user sources determine input presentation, including inputs recorded before a turn starts.
+
+Keyed Chat node renderers receive openView when hosted by the Conversation view. It selects a registered view with an opaque focus identity, so inspection links need not change Session history or navigate by DOM selectors.
+
+Feature-owned Chat nodes can set `independent: true` to remain outside both process groups and completed-turn disclosure. This keeps authored context visible without changing the ordinary context-message policy.
